---
import { SITE } from "../../data/site";

const localHour = Number(
  new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-GB", {
    hour: "2-digit",
    hour12: false,
    timeZone: SITE.timezone,
  }).format(new Date()),
);
const isAwake = localHour >= 8 && localHour < 23;
---

<section id="about" class="about-section">
  <div class="about-head">
    <h2 class="about-title font-display">
      Victor James. I go by vojmax.
    </h2>
  </div>

  <div class="about-body">
    <div class="about-portrait">
      <img src="/profile.png" alt="Victor James" class="portrait-img" />
      <span class="portrait-corner tl"></span>
      <span class="portrait-corner tr"></span>
      <span class="portrait-corner bl"></span>
      <span class="portrait-corner br"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="about-prose">
      <p>
        I started in design and ended up writing the code too. A lot of software
        falls apart at the seam between how it looks and how it works. Someone
        hands off a file, someone else interprets it, and the thing that ships is
        neither. I would rather hold both ends.
      </p>
      <p>
        I care about software that is clear about its limits. Several projects
        here carry a section on what they can't do or what their data can't
        account for. A forecast without an error bar is a guess in better
        clothing, and I would rather say so on the page than let someone find out
        later.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most of what I take on is a brand and the site it lives on: the name, the
        type system, the interaction, the deployment. Underneath that there is a
        second body of work that is mostly systems. Edge computer vision on
        Aegis, LAN file transfer on OctaneDrop, a desktop classifier on SFO, data
        pipelines on AgroSynapse. That work is why I can build the interfaces
        properly.
      </p>

      <dl class="about-facts">
        <div>
          <dt>Based in</dt>
          <dd>{SITE.location}</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Local time</dt>
          <dd>
            <span class={`tz-dot ${isAwake ? "awake" : "asleep"}`}></span>
            {isAwake ? "Probably awake" : "Probably asleep"}
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Working in</dt>
          <dd>TypeScript, Python, Rust</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Open to</dt>
          <dd>Brand and build work</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about-section {
    padding-block: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem) clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .about-head {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .about-title {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    line-height: 1.12;
    color: rgb(var(--text));
  }

  .about-body {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 260px) minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .about-body {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  /* Portrait */
  .about-portrait {
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: rgb(var(--panel2));
    border: 1px solid rgb(var(--border) / 0.1);
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .about-portrait {
      max-width: 240px;
    }
  }

  .portrait-img {
    height: 100%;
    width: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    filter: grayscale(0.25);
    transition: filter 0.4s ease;
  }

  .about-portrait:hover .portrait-img {
    filter: grayscale(0);
  }

  .portrait-corner {
    position: absolute;
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    border-color: rgb(var(--accent));
    border-style: solid;
    border-width: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .portrait-corner.tl {
    top: 10px;
    left: 10px;
    border-top-width: 2px;
    border-left-width: 2px;
  }
  .portrait-corner.tr {
    top: 10px;
    right: 10px;
    border-top-width: 2px;
    border-right-width: 2px;
  }
  .portrait-corner.bl {
    bottom: 10px;
    left: 10px;
    border-bottom-width: 2px;
    border-left-width: 2px;
  }
  .portrait-corner.br {
    bottom: 10px;
    right: 10px;
    border-bottom-width: 2px;
    border-right-width: 2px;
  }

  /* Prose */
  .about-prose p {
    margin: 0 0 1.15rem;
    max-width: 62ch;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: rgb(var(--text) / 0.82);
  }

  .about-prose p:last-of-type {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  /* Facts */
  .about-facts {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1px;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(11rem, 100%), 1fr));
    margin: 0;
    background: rgb(var(--border) / 0.1);
    border: 1px solid rgb(var(--border) / 0.1);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .about-facts > div {
    background: rgb(var(--panel));
    padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
  }

  .about-facts dt {
    margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgb(var(--muted));
  }

  .about-facts dd {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: rgb(var(--text));
  }

  .tz-dot {
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .tz-dot.awake {
    background: rgb(74 222 128);
  }

  .tz-dot.asleep {
    background: rgb(var(--muted));
  }
</style>
